{"id":"mahabharata-6-045","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":45,"title":"पञ्चचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 45 · First day: Bhishma drives back the Pandavas","summary":{"en":"In the afternoon Bhishma, guarded by Kripa, Shalya and others, rages through the Pandava army, and Arjuna and Bhima cannot stop him. The Pandava host breaks like a ship in a gale until sunset ends the day.","kn":"ಮಧ್ಯಾಹ್ನ ಕೃಪ, ಶಲ್ಯ ಮೊದಲಾದವರ ರಕ್ಷಣೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಭೀಷ್ಮನು ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಕೆರಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ, ಭೀಮರು ಅವನನ್ನು ತಡೆಯಲಾರರು. ಸೂರ್ಯಾಸ್ತದವರೆಗೆ ಪಾಂಡವಸೈನ್ಯ ಬಿರುಗಾಳಿಗೆ ಸಿಕ್ಕ ನಾವೆಯಂತೆ ಚದುರುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"अपराह्न में कृप, शल्य आदि से रक्षित भीष्म पाण्डव सेना में उग्र होते हैं और अर्जुन-भीम उन्हें रोक नहीं पाते। सूर्यास्त तक पाण्डव सेना आँधी में नाव की तरह बिखर जाती है।","te":"మధ్యాహ్నం కృపుడు, శల్యుడు మొదలైన వారి రక్షణలో భీష్ముడు పాండవసేనలో విజృంభిస్తాడు; అర్జునుడు, భీముడు అడ్డుకోలేరు. సూర్యాస్తమయం వరకు పాండవసేన తుఫానులో నావలా చెదిరిపోతుంది.","ta":"பிற்பகலில் கிருபர், சல்யர் முதலியோர் காக்க பீஷ்மர் பாண்டவப் படையில் சீறுகிறார்; அர்ஜுனனும் பீமனும் அவரைத் தடுக்க முடியவில்லை. புயலில் சிக்கிய கப்பல் போல் பாண்டவப் படை சிதறி, சூரிய அஸ்தமனத்தோடு அன்றைய போர் முடிகிறது.","ml":"ഉച്ചയ്ക്കുശേഷം കൃപർ, ശല്യർ തുടങ്ങിയവരുടെ സംരക്ഷണത്തിൽ ഭീഷ്മർ പാണ്ഡവ സേനയിൽ ആഞ്ഞടിക്കുന്നു; അർജുനനും ഭീമനും അദ്ദേഹത്തെ തടയാനാവുന്നില്ല. സൂര്യാസ്തമയം വരെ കൊടുങ്കാറ്റിൽപ്പെട്ട കപ്പൽപോലെ പാണ്ഡവ സേന തകരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.45; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"गतपूर्वाह्णभूयिष्ठे तस्मिन्नहनि दारुणे ।\nवर्तमाने महारौद्रे महावीरवरक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"When most of the morning of that terrible day had passed, and the dreadful slaughter of great heroes went on,"}},{"n":2,"text":"दुर्मुखः कृतवर्मा च कृपः शल्यो विविंशतिः ।\nभीष्मं जुगुपुरासाद्य तव पुत्रेण चोदिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Durmukha, Kritavarman, Kripa, Shalya and Vivimshati, urged by your son, came up and guarded Bhishma."}},{"n":3,"text":"एतैरतिरथैर्गुप्तः पञ्चभिर्भरतर्षभ ।\nपाण्डवानामनीकानि विजगाहे महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Protected by these five great chariot-warriors, O best of the Bharatas, the great warrior plunged into the Pandava divisions."}},{"n":4,"text":"चेदिकाशिकरूषेषु पाञ्चालेषु च भारत ।\nभीष्मस्य बहुधा तालश्चरन्केतुरदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the Chedis, Kashis and Karushas and the Panchalas, Bhishma's palm-tree banner was seen moving about in many places."}},{"n":5,"text":"शिरांसि च तदा भीष्मो बाहूंश्चापि सहायुधान् ।\nनिचकर्त महावेगैर्भल्लैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma then cut off heads and arms with their weapons, with swift, straight-jointed broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":6,"text":"नृत्यतो रथमार्गेषु भीष्मस्य भरतर्षभ ।\nकेचिदार्तस्वरं चक्रुर्नागा मर्मणि ताडिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Bhishma danced along the paths of his chariot, O best of the Bharatas, some elephants struck in the vitals cried out in pain."}},{"n":7,"text":"अभिमन्युः सुसंक्रुद्धः पिशङ्गैस्तुरगोत्तमैः ।\nसंयुक्तं रथमास्थाय प्रायाद्भीष्मरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abhimanyu, very angry, mounted a chariot yoked to excellent tawny horses and drove toward Bhishma's chariot."}},{"n":8,"text":"जाम्बूनदविचित्रेण कर्णिकारेण केतुना ।\nअभ्यवर्षत भीष्मं च तांश्चैव रथसत्तमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his banner of a golden karnikara tree he showered arrows on Bhishma and on those best of chariot-warriors."}},{"n":9,"text":"स तालकेतोस्तीक्ष्णेन केतुमाहत्य पत्रिणा ।\nभीष्मेण युयुधे वीरस्तस्य चानुचरैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"He struck the banner of the palm-tree-bannered Bhishma with a sharp feathered arrow, and the hero fought Bhishma and his followers."}},{"n":10,"text":"कृतवर्माणमेकेन शल्यं पञ्चभिरायसैः ।\nविद्ध्वा नवभिरानर्छच्छिताग्रैः प्रपितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Kritavarman with one arrow and Shalya with five iron ones, and wounded the great-grandfather Bhishma with nine sharp-pointed ones."}},{"n":11,"text":"पूर्णायतविसृष्टेन सम्यक्प्रणिहितेन च ।\nध्वजमेकेन विव्याध जाम्बूनदविभूषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With one arrow, well aimed and shot with a full draw, he pierced the banner adorned with gold."}},{"n":12,"text":"दुर्मुखस्य तु भल्लेन सर्वावरणभेदिना ।\nजहार सारथेः कायाच्छिरः संनतपर्वणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With one broad-headed arrow that cuts through all armor he cut off the head of Durmukha's charioteer from his body."}},{"n":13,"text":"धनुश्चिच्छेद भल्लेन कार्तस्वरविभूषितम् ।\nकृपस्य निशिताग्रेण तांश्च तीक्ष्णमुखैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a sharp-pointed broad-headed arrow he cut Kripa's bow, adorned with gold, and struck those others with sharp-headed arrows."}},{"n":14,"text":"जघान परमक्रुद्धो नृत्यन्निव महारथः ।\nतस्य लाघवमुद्वीक्ष्य तुतुषुर्देवता अपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Exceedingly angry, the great chariot-warrior seemed to dance; seeing his quickness, even the gods were pleased."}},{"n":15,"text":"लब्धलक्ष्यतया कार्ष्णेः सर्वे भीष्ममुखा रथाः ।\nसत्त्ववन्तममन्यन्त साक्षादिव धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because of Abhimanyu's accuracy, all those chariot-warriors led by Bhishma thought him mighty, almost like Dhananjaya himself."}},{"n":16,"text":"तस्य लाघवमार्गस्थमलातसदृशप्रभम् ।\nदिशः पर्यपतच्चापं गाण्डीवमिव घोषवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His bow, shining like a fire-brand, moved with his swift motion and flashed across the quarters, ringing like Gandiva."}},{"n":17,"text":"तमासाद्य महावेगैर्भीष्मो नवभिराशुगैः ।\nविव्याध समरे तूर्णमार्जुनिं परवीरहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, slayer of enemy heroes, approached Arjuna's son and quickly struck him in the battle with nine swift arrows."}},{"n":18,"text":"ध्वजं चास्य त्रिभिर्भल्लैश्चिच्छेद परमौजसः ।\nसारथिं च त्रिभिर्बाणैराजघान यतव्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The firm-vowed Bhishma cut his mighty banner with three broad-headed arrows and struck his charioteer with three arrows."}},{"n":19,"text":"तथैव कृतवर्मा च कृपः शल्यश्च मारिष ।\nविद्ध्वा नाकम्पयत्कार्ष्णिं मैनाकमिव पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise Kritavarman, Kripa and Shalya pierced Abhimanyu, but could not shake him, as one cannot shake Mount Mainaka."}},{"n":20,"text":"स तैः परिवृतः शूरो धार्तराष्ट्रैर्महारथैः ।\nववर्ष शरवर्षाणि कार्ष्णिः पञ्चरथान्प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by those great chariot-warriors of Dhritarashtra's side, the hero, Abhimanyu, rained showers of arrows on the five chariot-fighters."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततस्तेषां महास्त्राणि संवार्य शरवृष्टिभिः ।\nननाद बलवान्कार्ष्णिर्भीष्माय विसृजञ्शरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, checking their great weapons with his arrow-showers, the mighty Abhimanyu roared and shot arrows at Bhishma."}},{"n":22,"text":"तत्रास्य सुमहद्राजन्बाह्वोर्बलमदृश्यत ।\nयतमानस्य समरे भीष्ममर्दयतः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, great king, the great strength of his arms was seen as he strove in battle, tormenting Bhishma with arrows."}},{"n":23,"text":"पराक्रान्तस्य तस्यैव भीष्मोऽपि प्राहिणोच्छरान् ।\nस तांश्चिच्छेद समरे भीष्मचापच्युताञ्शरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma too sent arrows at the valiant youth, and Abhimanyu cut down in battle those arrows that had flown from Bhishma's bow."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततो ध्वजममोघेषुर्भीष्मस्य नवभिः शरैः ।\nचिच्छेद समरे वीरस्तत उच्चुक्रुशुर्जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the hero, whose arrows never missed, cut down Bhishma's banner with nine arrows, and people cried out."}},{"n":25,"text":"स राजतो महास्कन्धस्तालो हेमविभूषितः ।\nसौभद्रविशिखैश्छिन्नः पपात भुवि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"That silver palm tree with its great trunk, adorned with gold, cut by Subhadra's son's arrows, fell to the ground, O Bharata."}},{"n":26,"text":"ध्वजं सौभद्रविशिखैः पतितं भरतर्षभ ।\nदृष्ट्वा भीमोऽनदद्धृष्टः सौभद्रमभिहर्षयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the banner fall, cut by the arrows of Subhadra's son, O best of the Bharatas, Bhima roared in delight, gladdening Abhimanyu."}},{"n":27,"text":"अथ भीष्मो महास्त्राणि दिव्यानि च बहूनि च ।\nप्रादुश्चक्रे महारौद्रः क्षणे तस्मिन्महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the very fierce and mighty Bhishma at that moment displayed many great divine weapons."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततः शतसहस्रेण सौभद्रं प्रपितामहः ।\nअवाकिरदमेयात्मा शराणां नतपर्वणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great-grandfather, of immeasurable spirit, covered Subhadra's son with a hundred thousand straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततो दश महेष्वासाः पाण्डवानां महारथाः ।\nरक्षार्थमभ्यधावन्त सौभद्रं त्वरिता रथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then ten great archers, great chariot-warriors of the Pandavas, hurried in their chariots to protect Subhadra's son,"}},{"n":30,"text":"विराटः सह पुत्रेण धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पार्षतः ।\nभीमश्च केकयाश्चैव सात्यकिश्च विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"namely Virata with his son, Dhrishtadyumna, son of Prishata, Bhima, the Kekayas and Satyaki, lord of the people."}},{"n":31,"text":"जवेनापततां तेषां भीष्मः शांतनवो रणे ।\nपाञ्चाल्यं त्रिभिरानर्छत्सात्यकिं निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they rushed swiftly, Bhishma, son of Shantanu, struck the Panchala prince with three arrows and Satyaki with sharp arrows."}},{"n":32,"text":"पूर्णायतविसृष्टेन क्षुरेण निशितेन च ।\nध्वजमेकेन चिच्छेद भीमसेनस्य पत्रिणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a sharp razor-headed arrow, shot at full draw, he cut off Bhimasena's banner with one feathered shaft."}},{"n":33,"text":"जाम्बूनदमयः केतुः केसरी नरसत्तम ।\nपपात भीमसेनस्य भीष्मेण मथितो रथात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena's golden banner with the lion emblem, O best of men, fell from his chariot, shattered by Bhishma."}},{"n":34,"text":"भीमसेनस्त्रिभिर्विद्ध्वा भीष्मं शांतनवं रणे ।\nकृपमेकेन विव्याध कृतवर्माणमष्टभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena pierced Bhishma, son of Shantanu, with three arrows in battle, Kripa with one, and Kritavarman with eight."}},{"n":35,"text":"प्रगृहीताग्रहस्तेन वैराटिरपि दन्तिना ।\nअभ्यद्रवत राजानं मद्राधिपतिमुत्तरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Virata's son Uttara, with an elephant whose trunk-tip was lifted high, rushed at the king, the lord of Madra, Shalya."}},{"n":36,"text":"तस्य वारणराजस्य जवेनापततो रथी ।\nशल्यो निवारयामास वेगमप्रतिमं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that king of elephants rushed in speed, Shalya in his chariot checked its peerless force in battle."}},{"n":37,"text":"तस्य क्रुद्धः स नागेन्द्रो बृहतः साधुवाहिनः ।\nपदा युगमधिष्ठाय जघान चतुरो हयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angered, that lord of elephants, huge and well-trained, put its foot on the chariot yoke and killed Shalya's four horses."}},{"n":38,"text":"स हताश्वे रथे तिष्ठन्मद्राधिपतिरायसीम् ।\nउत्तरान्तकरीं शक्तिं चिक्षेप भुजगोपमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Standing in his chariot with its horses dead, the lord of Madra hurled an iron spear, like a snake, that could end Uttara."}},{"n":39,"text":"तया भिन्नतनुत्राणः प्रविश्य विपुलं तमः ।\nस पपात गजस्कन्धात्प्रमुक्ताङ्कुशतोमरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its blow tore Uttara's armor and he, entering a vast darkness, fell from the elephant's shoulder, letting go of his goad and spear."}},{"n":40,"text":"समादाय च शल्योऽसिमवप्लुत्य रथोत्तमात् ।\nवारणेन्द्रस्य विक्रम्य चिच्छेदाथ महाकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya took a sword, leaped down from the fine chariot, and boldly cut off the great trunk of the lord of elephants."}},{"n":41,"text":"भिन्नमर्मा शरव्रातैश्छिन्नहस्तः स वारणः ।\nभीममार्तस्वरं कृत्वा पपात च ममार च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its vitals pierced by showers of arrows and its trunk cut off, the elephant gave a terrible cry of pain, fell, and died."}},{"n":42,"text":"एतदीदृशकं कृत्वा मद्रराजो महारथः ।\nआरुरोह रथं तूर्णं भास्वरं कृतवर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having done this, the great chariot-warrior, the king of Madra, quickly climbed onto Kritavarman's shining chariot."}},{"n":43,"text":"उत्तरं निहतं दृष्ट्वा वैराटिर्भ्रातरं शुभम् ।\nकृतवर्मणा च सहितं दृष्ट्वा शल्यमवस्थितम् ।\nशङ्खः क्रोधात्प्रजज्वाल हविषा हव्यवाडिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his fine brother Uttara killed, and seeing Shalya standing with Kritavarman, Virata's son Shankha blazed with anger, like a fire fed with oblation."}},{"n":44,"text":"स विस्फार्य महच्चापं कार्तस्वरविभूषितम् ।\nअभ्यधावज्जिघांसन्वै शल्यं मद्राधिपं बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty one, stretching his great bow adorned with gold, rushed at Shalya, the lord of Madra, wishing to kill him."}},{"n":45,"text":"महता रथवंशेन समन्तात्परिवारितः ।\nसृजन्बाणमयं वर्षं प्रायाच्छल्यरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded on all sides by a great line of chariots, he went toward Shalya's chariot, pouring out a rain of arrows."}},{"n":46,"text":"तमापतन्तं संप्रेक्ष्य मत्तवारणविक्रमम् ।\nतावकानां रथाः सप्त समन्तात्पर्यवारयन् ।\nमद्रराजं परीप्सन्तो मृत्योर्दंष्ट्रान्तरं गतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him come on with the force of a rutting elephant, seven of your chariot-warriors surrounded him on every side, wishing to save the king of Madra, who had come between the jaws of death."}},{"n":47,"text":"ततो भीष्मो महाबाहुर्विनद्य जलदो यथा ।\nतालमात्रं धनुर्गृह्य शङ्खमभ्यद्रवद्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty-armed Bhishma, roaring like a cloud, took up a bow as long as a palm tree and rushed at Shankha in the battle."}},{"n":48,"text":"तमुद्यतमुदीक्ष्याथ महेष्वासं महाबलम् ।\nसंत्रस्ता पाण्डवी सेना वातवेगहतेव नौः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that mighty archer, so strong, raised against him, the Pandava army was terrified, like a ship struck by a gale."}},{"n":49,"text":"तत्रार्जुनः संत्वरितः शङ्खस्यासीत्पुरःसरः ।\nभीष्माद्रक्ष्योऽयमद्येति ततो युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna hurried then and went in front of Shankha, thinking \"He must be protected from Bhishma today,\" and then the fighting began."}},{"n":50,"text":"हाहाकारो महानासीद्योधानां युधि युध्यताम् ।\nतेजस्तेजसि संपृक्तमित्येवं विस्मयं ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great cry of dismay went up from the warriors fighting in the battle. \"Radiance is meeting radiance!\" they said in wonder."}},{"n":51,"text":"अथ शल्यो गदापाणिरवतीर्य महारथात् ।\nशङ्खस्य चतुरो वाहानहनद्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shalya, mace in hand, got down from his great chariot and killed Shankha's four horses, O best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":52,"text":"स हताश्वाद्रथात्तूर्णं खड्गमादाय विद्रुतः ।\nबीभत्सोः स्यन्दनं प्राप्य ततः शान्तिमविन्दत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Quickly leaving his chariot, its horses dead, and taking a sword, Shankha fled, and reaching the chariot of Bibhatsu, found safety."}},{"n":53,"text":"ततो भीष्मरथात्तूर्णमुत्पतन्ति पतत्रिणः ।\nयैरन्तरिक्षं भूमिश्च सर्वतः समवस्तृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then from Bhishma's chariot feathered arrows flew up quickly, and covered the sky and earth on every side."}},{"n":54,"text":"पाञ्चालानथ मत्स्यांश्च केकयांश्च प्रभद्रकान् ।\nभीष्मः प्रहरतां श्रेष्ठः पातयामास मार्गणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, best of strikers, felled with his arrows the Panchalas, Matsyas, Kekayas and Prabhadrakas."}},{"n":55,"text":"उत्सृज्य समरे तूर्णं पाण्डवं सव्यसाचिनम् ।\nअभ्यद्रवत पाञ्चाल्यं द्रुपदं सेनया वृतम् ।\nप्रियं संबन्धिनं राजञ्शरानवकिरन्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving the Pandava Savyasachin in the battle, he quickly rushed at Drupada, the Panchala, surrounded by his army, his dear kinsman by marriage, showering many arrows, O king."}},{"n":56,"text":"अग्निनेव प्रदग्धानि वनानि शिशिरात्यये ।\nशरदग्धान्यदृश्यन्त सैन्यानि द्रुपदस्य ह ।\nअतिष्ठत रणे भीष्मो विधूम इव पावकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like forests burnt by fire at the end of winter, Drupada's armies were seen scorched by arrows, while Bhishma stood in the battle like a smokeless fire."}},{"n":57,"text":"मध्यंदिने यथादित्यं तपन्तमिव तेजसा ।\nन शेकुः पाण्डवेयस्य योधा भीष्मं निरीक्षितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava's warriors could not look at Bhishma, who blazed like the midday sun with his radiance."}},{"n":58,"text":"वीक्षां चक्रुः समन्तात्ते पाण्डवा भयपीडिताः ।\nत्रातारं नाध्यगच्छन्त गावः शीतार्दिता इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, afflicted by fear, looked all around and found no protector, like cattle tormented by cold."}},{"n":59,"text":"हतविप्रद्रुते सैन्ये निरुत्साहे विमर्दिते ।\nहाहाकारो महानासीत्पाण्डुसैन्येषु भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the army slain, scattered, disheartened and crushed, a great cry of dismay went up among the Pandava forces, O Bharata."}},{"n":60,"text":"ततो भीष्मः शांतनवो नित्यं मण्डलकार्मुकः ।\nमुमोच बाणान्दीप्ताग्रानहीनाशीविषानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma, son of Shantanu, who always held his bow in a full circle, loosed arrows with blazing tips, like venomous snakes."}},{"n":61,"text":"शरैरेकायनीकुर्वन्दिशः सर्वा यतव्रतः ।\nजघान पाण्डवरथानादिश्यादिश्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Firm in his vows, he made all the directions a single path with his arrows and struck down the Pandava chariots one after another, pointing at each, O Bharata."}},{"n":62,"text":"ततः सैन्येषु भग्नेषु मथितेषु च सर्वशः ।\nप्राप्ते चास्तं दिनकरे न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with the armies broken and crushed on every side, as the sun was setting, nothing could be made out."}},{"n":63,"text":"भीष्मं च समुदीर्यन्तं दृष्ट्वा पार्था महाहवे ।\nअवहारमकुर्वन्त सैन्यानां भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Bhishma rising high in that great battle, the sons of Pritha, O best of the Bharatas, called off their armies."}}]}]}